"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013116650259522942,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.044120003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":29.4,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bowhead Specialty Holdings Inc. provides commercial specialty property and casualty insurance products in the United States. It underwrites casualty insurance solutions for risks in the construction, distribution, heavy manufacturing, real estate, and hospitality segments; professional liability insurance solutions, including directors and officers liability, errors and omissions liability, employment practices liability, fiduciary liability, fidelity liability and miscellaneous professional liability, crime insurance, and cyber for financial institutions; and healthcare solutions for hospitals, senior care providers, managed care organizations, miscellaneous medical facilities, and management liability segments. In addition, it offers Baleen Specialty, a technology-powered underwriting operation, that specializes in small to mid-sized risks that are not eligible in the admitted market. It distributes its products through distribution partners in wholesale and retail markets. The company was formerly known as Bowhead Holdings Inc. and changed its name to Bowhead Specialty Holdings Inc. in March 2024. The company was founded in 2020 and is based in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen Jay Sills | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 77 | Compensation: $1.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 296 people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $1.1M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $24K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Bowhead Specialty Holdings Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.1B market cap on $552M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +30% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 15% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $326M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 59 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 6.16\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 34\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 17% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.5478595478595489},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 79% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Unum Group (NYSE:UNM) and Bowhead Specialty (NYSE:BOW) Critical Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/unum-group-nyseunm-and-bowhead-specialty-nysebow-critical-review.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403734.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.914,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Technical Reactions to BOW Trends in Macro Strategies","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_